# Root .gitignore.
#
# The three Python subprojects keep their own (PythonWorker/, CarDetection/,
# RoadDamage/); this file covers the repo root and the Xcode project.

# Claude-written markdown — kept local, not shared.
#
# Note for whoever clones this next: the repo's working rules, its ADR record and
# its what's-real-vs-mock status all live in these files, so a fresh clone gets
# none of that context. The architecture reasoning they carry (ADR-015/016: why
# road damage ships boxes not segmentation, why severity is computed only in
# Python, why there are three incompatible venvs) is not recoverable from the
# diff. Ask the repo owner for a copy rather than reconstructing it.
CLAUDE.md
JOURNAL.md
PROGRESS.md
ROAD_DAMAGE_BRIEF.md
.claude